{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "kjv-ephesians-005",
  "collection": "kjv-bible",
  "document_type": "bible_chapter",
  "number": 5,
  "title": "Ephesians 5",
  "display_title": "Ephesians 5",
  "translation": "King James Version",
  "translationCode": "KJV",
  "bookId": "ephesians",
  "book": "Ephesians",
  "bookName": "Ephesians",
  "bookOrder": 49,
  "testament": "new",
  "chapter": 5,
  "sortOrder": 49005,
  "verseCount": 33,
  "aliases": [
    "Eph",
    "Ephes"
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:ephesians:5:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "Be ye therefore followers of God, as dear children;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ephesians 5:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ephesians:5:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:ephesians:5:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "And walk in love, as Christ also hath loved us, and hath given himself for us an offering and a sacrifice to God for a sweetsmelling savour.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ephesians 5:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ephesians:5:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:ephesians:5:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "But fornication, and all uncleanness, or covetousness, let it not be once named among you, as becometh saints;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ephesians 5:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ephesians:5:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:ephesians:5:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "Neither filthiness, nor foolish talking, nor jesting, which are not convenient: but rather giving of thanks.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ephesians 5:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ephesians:5:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:ephesians:5:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "For this ye know, that no whoremonger, nor unclean person, nor covetous man, who is an idolater, hath any inheritance in the kingdom of Christ and of God.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ephesians 5:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ephesians:5:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:ephesians:5:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "Let no man deceive you with vain words: for because of these things cometh the wrath of God upon the children of disobedience.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ephesians 5:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ephesians:5:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:ephesians:5:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "Be not ye therefore partakers with them.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ephesians 5:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ephesians:5:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:ephesians:5:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "For ye were sometimes darkness, but now are ye light in the Lord: walk as children of light:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ephesians 5:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ephesians:5:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:ephesians:5:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "(For the fruit of the Spirit is in all goodness and righteousness and truth;)",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ephesians 5:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ephesians:5:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:ephesians:5:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "Proving what is acceptable unto the Lord.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ephesians 5:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ephesians:5:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:ephesians:5:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "And have no fellowship with the unfruitful works of darkness, but rather reprove them.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ephesians 5:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ephesians:5:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:ephesians:5:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "For it is a shame even to speak of those things which are done of them in secret.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ephesians 5:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ephesians:5:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:ephesians:5:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "But all things that are reproved are made manifest by the light: for whatsoever doth make manifest is light.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ephesians 5:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ephesians:5:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:ephesians:5:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "Wherefore he saith, Awake thou that sleepest, and arise from the dead, and Christ shall give thee light.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ephesians 5:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ephesians:5:14"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-015",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 15,
      "verseId": "kjv:ephesians:5:15",
      "numberLabel": "15",
      "text": "See then that ye walk circumspectly, not as fools, but as wise,",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ephesians 5:15",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ephesians:5:15"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-016",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 16,
      "verseId": "kjv:ephesians:5:16",
      "numberLabel": "16",
      "text": "Redeeming the time, because the days are evil.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ephesians 5:16",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ephesians:5:16"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-017",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 17,
      "verseId": "kjv:ephesians:5:17",
      "numberLabel": "17",
      "text": "Wherefore be ye not unwise, but understanding what the will of the Lord is.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ephesians 5:17",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ephesians:5:17"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-018",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 18,
      "verseId": "kjv:ephesians:5:18",
      "numberLabel": "18",
      "text": "And be not drunk with wine, wherein is excess; but be filled with the Spirit;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ephesians 5:18",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ephesians:5:18"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-019",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 19,
      "verseId": "kjv:ephesians:5:19",
      "numberLabel": "19",
      "text": "Speaking to yourselves in psalms and hymns and spiritual songs, singing and making melody in your heart to the Lord;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ephesians 5:19",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ephesians:5:19"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-020",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 20,
      "verseId": "kjv:ephesians:5:20",
      "numberLabel": "20",
      "text": "Giving thanks always for all things unto God and the Father in the name of our Lord Jesus Christ;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ephesians 5:20",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ephesians:5:20"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-021",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 21,
      "verseId": "kjv:ephesians:5:21",
      "numberLabel": "21",
      "text": "Submitting yourselves one to another in the fear of God.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ephesians 5:21",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ephesians:5:21"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-022",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 22,
      "verseId": "kjv:ephesians:5:22",
      "numberLabel": "22",
      "text": "Wives, submit yourselves unto your own husbands, as unto the Lord.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ephesians 5:22",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ephesians:5:22"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-023",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 23,
      "verseId": "kjv:ephesians:5:23",
      "numberLabel": "23",
      "text": "For the husband is the head of the wife, even as Christ is the head of the church: and he is the saviour of the body.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ephesians 5:23",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ephesians:5:23"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-024",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 24,
      "verseId": "kjv:ephesians:5:24",
      "numberLabel": "24",
      "text": "Therefore as the church is subject unto Christ, so let the wives be to their own husbands in every thing.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ephesians 5:24",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ephesians:5:24"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-025",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 25,
      "verseId": "kjv:ephesians:5:25",
      "numberLabel": "25",
      "text": "Husbands, love your wives, even as Christ also loved the church, and gave himself for it;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ephesians 5:25",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ephesians:5:25"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-026",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 26,
      "verseId": "kjv:ephesians:5:26",
      "numberLabel": "26",
      "text": "That he might sanctify and cleanse it with the washing of water by the word,",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ephesians 5:26",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ephesians:5:26"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-027",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 27,
      "verseId": "kjv:ephesians:5:27",
      "numberLabel": "27",
      "text": "That he might present it to himself a glorious church, not having spot, or wrinkle, or any such thing; but that it should be holy and without blemish.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ephesians 5:27",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ephesians:5:27"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-028",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 28,
      "verseId": "kjv:ephesians:5:28",
      "numberLabel": "28",
      "text": "So ought men to love their wives as their own bodies. He that loveth his wife loveth himself.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ephesians 5:28",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ephesians:5:28"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-029",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 29,
      "verseId": "kjv:ephesians:5:29",
      "numberLabel": "29",
      "text": "For no man ever yet hated his own flesh; but nourisheth and cherisheth it, even as the Lord the church:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ephesians 5:29",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ephesians:5:29"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-030",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 30,
      "verseId": "kjv:ephesians:5:30",
      "numberLabel": "30",
      "text": "For we are members of his body, of his flesh, and of his bones.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ephesians 5:30",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ephesians:5:30"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-031",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 31,
      "verseId": "kjv:ephesians:5:31",
      "numberLabel": "31",
      "text": "For this cause shall a man leave his father and mother, and shall be joined unto his wife, and they two shall be one flesh.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ephesians 5:31",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ephesians:5:31"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-032",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 32,
      "verseId": "kjv:ephesians:5:32",
      "numberLabel": "32",
      "text": "This is a great mystery: but I speak concerning Christ and the church.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ephesians 5:32",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ephesians:5:32"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-033",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 33,
      "verseId": "kjv:ephesians:5:33",
      "numberLabel": "33",
      "text": "Nevertheless let every one of you in particular so love his wife even as himself; and the wife see that she reverence her husband.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ephesians 5:33",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ephesians:5:33"
      }
    }
  ],
